# Owner review for the files that decide whether CI can fail, for the generated
# ledger and its generator, and for the contract itself.
#
# AGENTS.md ("Tests, workflows, manifests, baseline changes, and
# security-critical code require independent review") and ADR-002 § "Branch
# protection and rulesets" (item 7) require owner review on workflows, gate
# scripts and the required-check manifest. A manifest edited in the same PR as
# the thing it guards defeats the gate, which is exactly what this file exists
# to prevent.
#
# NOTHING ENFORCES THIS FILE TODAY. CODEOWNERS is advisory until a ruleset
# requires owner review on these paths. Applying that ruleset is an owner action
# after this PR lands (ADR-002 item 9: "application happens after PR1 lands,
# because ci-required must exist before it can be required"), and GitHub
# rulesets return 403 on this repository's current plan. So this file records
# the intended ownership; it does not currently block anything.

# Everything in this repository, as the baseline.
*                            @yegamble

# CI definition, the required-check manifest and the fan-in gate.
/.github/                    @yegamble

# The gate scripts: they decide what red means.
/scripts/                    @yegamble

# The shared engineering contract.
/AGENTS.md                   @yegamble

# Accepted architecture decisions.
/docs/adr/                   @yegamble

# The generated ledger and the release profiles read from it.
/docs/quality/               @yegamble

# The ledger's SOURCE. docs/quality/features.json is generated from here, so
# review on the JSON alone would miss the change that produces it.
/docs/evidence/ledger-generator/   @yegamble

# Agent configuration: war-room roles, skills and permissions.
/.claude/                    @yegamble
